  "content": "<div class=\"page-links\">Pages: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">1</span></a> <span class=\"post-page-numbers current\" aria-current=\"page\"><span class=\"page-link\">2</span></span> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/3/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">3</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/4/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">4</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/5/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">5</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/6/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">6</span></a></div><div id=\"ez-toc-container\" class=\"ez-toc-v2_0_89 ez-toc-wrap-right counter-hierarchy ez-toc-counter ez-toc-grey ez-toc-container-direction\"><div class=\"ez-toc-title-container\"><p class=\"ez-toc-title\" style=\"cursor:inherit\">Contents</p>\n<span class=\"ez-toc-title-toggle\"><a href=\"#\" class=\"ez-toc-pull-right ez-toc-btn ez-toc-btn-xs ez-toc-btn-default ez-toc-toggle\" aria-label=\"Toggle Table of Content\"><span class=\"ez-toc-js-icon-con\"><span class=\"\"><span class=\"eztoc-hide\" style=\"display:none;\">Toggle</span><span class=\"ez-toc-icon-toggle-span\"><svg style=\"fill: #999;color:#999\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"list-377408\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M6 6H4v2h2V6zm14 0H8v2h12V6zM4 11h2v2H4v-2zm16 0H8v2h12v-2zM4 16h2v2H4v-2zm16 0H8v2h12v-2z\" fill=\"currentColor\"></path></svg><svg style=\"fill: #999;color:#999\" class=\"arrow-unsorted-368013\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10px\" height=\"10px\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" version=\"1.2\" baseProfile=\"tiny\"><path d=\"M18.2 9.3l-6.2-6.3-6.2 6.3c-.2.2-.3.4-.3.7s.1.5.3.7c.2.2.4.3.7.3h11c.3 0 .5-.1.7-.3.2-.2.3-.5.3-.7s-.1-.5-.3-.7zM5.8 14.7l6.2 6.3 6.2-6.3c.2-.2.3-.5.3-.7s-.1-.5-.3-.7c-.2-.2-.4-.3-.7-.3h-11c-.3 0-.5.1-.7.3-.2.2-.3.5-.3.7s.1.5.3.7z\"/></svg></span></span></span></a></span></div><nav><ul class='ez-toc-list ez-toc-list-level-1 eztoc-toggle-hide-by-default' ><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-1\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/#Personnel\" >Personnel</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-2\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/#Tracklisting\" >Tracklisting</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-3\" href=\"#In_the_studio\" >In the studio</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-4\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/3/#Innovations\" >Innovations</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-5\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/4/#The_medley\" >The medley</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-6\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/4/#The_title\" >The title</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-7\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/5/#The_cover_artwork\" >The cover artwork</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-8\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/5/#Paul_is_dead\" >\u2019Paul is dead&#8217;</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-9\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/6/#The_legacy\" >The legacy</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-10\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/6/#Chart_success\" >Chart success</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-11\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/6/#SomethingCome_Together\" >Something/Come Together</a></li></ul></nav></div><h2><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"In_the_studio\"></span>In the studio<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2><p>Although The Beatles business problems needed attention daily, and tempers within the group could be fractious, when they came together in the studio the bond between them was as strong as ever. A year after <em>Abbey Road</em>\u2019s release, at a time when the former Beatles were bitterly divided, <a href=\"/people/john-lennon/\">John Lennon</a> acknowledged how they understood one another as musicians.</p><blockquote><div>In spite of all the things\u2026 the Beatles really could play music together when they weren&#8217;t uptight. And if I get a thing going, <a href=\"/people/ringo-starr/\">Ringo</a> knows where to go. Like <em>that</em>. We&#8217;ve played together so long that it fits. That&#8217;s the only thing I sometimes miss is, is being able to just sort of blink or make a certain noise and I know they&#8217;ll all know where we&#8217;re going on an ad lib thing.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">John Lennon, 1970<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/lennonremembers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Lennon Remembers</em></a>, Jann S Wenner</div><p>The Beatles began 1969 with rehearsals and recording in Twickenham Film Studios and the basement of Apple&#8217;s office building. After the <a href=\"/albums/let-it-be/\"><em>Let It Be</em></a> sessions they also recorded at Trident and Olympic studios in London, but from May 1969 onwards worked exclusively at EMI Studios on Abbey Road, London.</p><blockquote><div>During the album things got a bit more positive and, although it had some overdubs, we got to play the whole medley. We put them in order, played the backing track and recorded it all in one take, going from one arrangement to the next. We did actually perform more like musicians again.</p><p>Likewise with the vocal tracks: we had to rehearse a lot of harmonies and learn all the back-up parts. Some songs are good with just one voice and then harmonies coming in at different places and sometimes three-part work. It&#8217;s just embellishment, really, and I suppose we made up parts where we thought it fitted because we were all trying to be singers then.</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\"><a href=\"/people/george-harrison/\">George Harrison</a><br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><p>While the album was recorded after the <a href=\"/features/get-back-let-it-be-sessions-complete-song-list/\">January 1969 sessions</a> for <em>Let It Be</em>, there was no clear date for the beginning of the <em>Abbey Road</em> project. The songs were begun while work continued on <em>Let It Be</em>, and recording for <em>Abbey Road</em> only properly began in April 1969.</p><p>The Beatles performed early versions of 12 of the <em>Abbey Road</em> songs during the <em>Let It Be</em> sessions. The only songs not to have been performed in any form were <a href=\"/songs/come-together/\">&#8216;Come Together&#8217;</a>, <a href=\"/songs/here-comes-the-sun/\">&#8216;Here Comes The Sun&#8217;</a>, <a href=\"/songs/because/\">&#8216;Because&#8217;</a>, <a href=\"/songs/you-never-give-me-your-money/\">&#8216;You Never Give Me Your Money&#8217;</a>, and <a href=\"/songs/the-end/\">&#8216;The End&#8217;</a>.</p><div class=\"epyt-video-wrapper\"><iframe  id=\"_ytid_85246\"  width=\"580\" height=\"435\"  data-origwidth=\"580\" data-origheight=\"435\"  data-relstop=\"1\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/BpndGZ71yww?enablejsapi=1&#038;autoplay=0&#038;cc_load_policy=0&#038;cc_lang_pref=&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;loop=0&#038;rel=0&#038;fs=1&#038;playsinline=0&#038;autohide=2&#038;theme=dark&#038;color=red&#038;controls=1&#038;disablekb=0&#038;\" class=\"__youtube_prefs__  epyt-is-override  no-lazyload\" title=\"YouTube player\"  allow=\"fullscreen; accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen data-no-lazy=\"1\" data-skipgform_ajax_framebjll=\"\"></iframe></div><p>Others had been written well before 1969. <a href=\"/1968/05/24/demo-recordings-for-the-white-album/\">Demo recordings</a> of <a href=\"/songs/mean-mr-mustard/\">&#8216;Mean Mr Mustard&#8217;</a> and <a href=\"/songs/polythene-pam/\">&#8216;Polythene Pam&#8217;</a> were made at George Harrison&#8217;s house in May 1968, following The Beatles&#8217; return from studying Transcendental Meditation with <a href=\"/people/maharishi-mahesh-yogi/\">Maharishi Mahesh Yogi</a> in <a href=\"/features/india/\">India</a>.</p><blockquote><div>My contribution [to the medley] is &#8216;Polythene Pam&#8217;, <a href=\"/songs/sun-king/\">&#8216;Sun King&#8217;</a> and Mean Mr Mustard. We juggled them about until it made vague sense. In &#8216;Mean Mr Mustard&#8217;, I said &#8216;his sister Pam&#8217; \u2013 originally it was &#8216;his sister Shirley&#8217; in the lyric. I changed it to &#8216;Pam&#8217; to make it sound like it had something to do with it. They are only finished bits of crap that I wrote in India.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">John Lennon, 1969<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><div data-carousel-extra='{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/&quot;}' id='gallery-1' class='gallery galleryid-28 gallery-columns-2 gallery-size-thumbnail'><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/69_paul-mccartney-george-harrison_01/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxNTUiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTU1IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"155\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_paul-mccartney-george-harrison_01-155x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Paul McCartney and George Harrison recording Abbey Road, 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_paul-mccartney-george-harrison_01-155x200.jpg 155w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_paul-mccartney-george-harrison_01-451x580.jpg 451w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_paul-mccartney-george-harrison_01.jpg 523w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 155px) 100vw, 155px\" data-attachment-id=\"48449\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/69_paul-mccartney-george-harrison_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_paul-mccartney-george-harrison_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"523,673\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-comments-count=\"6\" data-image-title=\"Paul McCartney and George Harrison recording Abbey Road, 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_paul-mccartney-george-harrison_01.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/69_john-lennon_002/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTI4IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEyOCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"128\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_002-200x128.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"John Lennon recording Abbey Road, 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_002-200x128.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_002-580x372.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_002-768x492.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_002.jpg 893w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"48450\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/69_john-lennon_002/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_002.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"893,572\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"John Lennon recording Abbey Road, 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_002.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/69_george-harrison_01/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTM0IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEzNCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"134\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_george-harrison_01-200x134.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George Harrison recording Abbey Road, 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_george-harrison_01-200x134.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_george-harrison_01-580x388.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_george-harrison_01-768x514.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_george-harrison_01.jpg 884w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"48447\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/69_george-harrison_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_george-harrison_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"884,592\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George Harrison recording Abbey Road, 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_george-harrison_01.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/69_john-lennon_003/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTMyIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEzMiI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"132\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_003-200x132.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"John Lennon recording Abbey Road, 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_003-200x132.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_003-580x384.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_003-768x508.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_003.jpg 884w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"48448\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/69_john-lennon_003/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_003.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"884,585\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"John Lennon recording Abbey Road, 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_john-lennon_003.jpg\" /></a></div></figure></div><p>The first <em>Abbey Road</em> song to be properly recorded in the studio, as opposed to rehearsals at Twickenham or Apple, was John Lennon&#8217;s <a href=\"/songs/i-want-you-shes-so-heavy/\">&#8216;I Want You (She&#8217;s So Heavy)&#8217;</a>. Work on the song began on <a href=\"/1969/02/22/recording-i-want-you-shes-so-heavy/\">22 February 1969</a> at Trident Studios in London, although at this time it was unclear whether the song would be an album track or appear on a single.</p><p>As the sessions progressed, they also cut non-album tracks <a href=\"/songs/the-ballad-of-john-and-yoko/\">&#8216;The Ballad Of John And Yoko&#8217;</a> and <a href=\"/songs/old-brown-shoe/\">Old Brown Shoe, readied the </a><a href=\"/songs/get-back/\">&#8216;Get Back&#8217;</a>/<a href=\"/songs/dont-let-me-down/\">&#8216;Don&#8217;t Let Me Down&#8217;</a> single, and oversaw the editing and mixing of the <em>Let It Be</em> tapes. Of the <em>Abbey Road</em> songs, The Beatles also worked on <a href=\"/songs/something/\">&#8216;Something&#8217;</a>, <a href=\"/songs/oh-darling/\">&#8216;Oh! Darling&#8217;</a>, <a href=\"/songs/octopuss-garden/\">&#8216;Octopus&#8217;s Garden&#8217;</a> and <a href=\"/songs/you-never-give-me-your-money/\">&#8216;You Never Give Me Your Money&#8217;</a>, before taking the month of June 1969 off for holidays.</p><blockquote><div><em>Let It Be</em> was such an unhappy record, even though there are some great songs on it, that I really believed that was the end of The Beatles, and I assumed that I would never work with them again. I thought, &#8216;What a shame to end like this.&#8217; So I was quite surprised when <a href=\"/people/paul-mccartney/\">Paul</a> rang me up and said, &#8216;We&#8217;re going to make another record \u2013 would you like to produce it?&#8217;</p><p>My immediate answer was: &#8216;Only if you let me produce it the way we used to.&#8217; He said, &#8216;We will, we want to.&#8217; \u2013 &#8216;John included?&#8217; \u2013 &#8216;Yes, honestly.&#8217; So I said, &#8216;Well, if you really want to, let&#8217;s do it. Let&#8217;s get together again.&#8217; It was a very happy record. I guess it was happy because everybody thought it was going to be the last.</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\"><a href=\"/people/george-martin/\">George Martin</a><br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><p>When The Beatles regrouped in July they worked swiftly to complete the record. Studio Two at EMI Studios was block-booked between 2.30pm and 10pm from <a href=\"/1969/07/01/recording-you-never-give-me-your-money/\">1 July</a> to 29 August, with the group committed to making the recordings worthwhile.</p><p>John Lennon missed the first of these sessions, having injured himself in a <a href=\"/1969/07/01/john-lennon-crashes-his-car-in-scotland/\">car crash in Scotland</a> on 1 July. He never intended to attend the first session of the month, but the crash and his subsequent hospitalisation and recuperation meant The Beatles worked without him until <a href=\"/1969/07/09/recording-maxwells-silver-hammer/\">9 July</a>.</p><div data-carousel-extra='{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/abbey-road/&quot;}' id='gallery-2' class='gallery galleryid-28 gallery-columns-2 gallery-size-thumbnail'><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/69_pattie-boyd-mal-evans-linda-mccartney-yoko-ono_01/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTk4IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDE5OCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"198\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_pattie-boyd-mal-evans-linda-mccartney-yoko-ono_01-200x198.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Pattie Boyd, Mal Evans, Linda McCartney and Yoko Ono at EMI Studios, 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/69_pattie-boyd-mal-evans-linda-mccartney-yoko-ono_01-200x198.jp